  "source": "Windows \"Arabic (101)\", from Unicode CLDR 43 keyboard data (Unicode License v3), with the Quranic marks added by us on AltGr. AltGr on a key gives the Quranic form of the mark on its Shift (AltGr+Q the dagger alif \u0670, AltGr+X the Quranic sukun \u06E1, AltGr+W, R and S the open tanwin), AltGr+H types ٱ, the number row the pause marks, ۞, ﴿ ﴾, \u06DD and ۩, and Shift+AltGr the Arabic-Indic digits.",
